#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-AD0047 expect=violation domain=ADAE
#note "PLAN-library-template-label-resolution round-2 T2 review H1, on OUR metadata store: ADAE under the D10-inferred OCCDS 1.0 (base Req STUDYID, USUBJID, --SEQ, --TERM, CMTRT, AESER) with NO AESEQ column, so no source domain is confirmed. The '--' names are not demanded (R2-1 (i): the concrete variable cannot be named), CMTRT carries the CM prefix and ADAE gives no CM evidence (no CMSEQ) so it is not demanded either; but AESER carries ADAE's own AD<domain> candidate AE and stays demanded (R2-1 (ii) drops only a name carrying ANOTHER domain's prefix) -> one violation naming exactly AESER. Before the fix the unconfirmed domain dropped AESER too, so the missing AESEQ disarmed its sibling's requirement and the dataset passed."
#library-ref standard=adamig version=1-1
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt "$missing_required_variables"="[AESER]"
dataset ADAE
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col AETERM type=Char label="Reported Term for the Adverse Event"
col AEDECOD type=Char label="Dictionary-Derived Term"
---
CDISCPILOT01 | 01-701-1015 | HEADACHE | HEADACHE
---
